    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n27268" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διορθ-ωτής</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οῦ</span>,
			ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>a corrector,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῶν σοφῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					LXX
					<u>Wi.</u>
					7.15
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῆς πολιτείας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Sol.</u>
					16
				</span></i>
			; = Lat. <i>corrector civitatium,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Arr.
				<u>Epict.</u>
				3.7.1
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> esp. <i>of
				books, editor, reviser,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				D.S.
				15.6
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				8.758
			</span></i>.</div>
